.TH EDITCONTROLS 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 Emulator 26.02.18" "Vircon32 Emulator"
.SH NAME
EditControls \- configure Vircon32 emulator keyboard and joystick controls
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B EditControls
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B EditControls
is the graphical companion to
.BR Vircon32 (1)
for mapping the host's keyboard and joysticks onto the Vircon32
gamepad: a D-pad, buttons A, B, X, Y, L and R, and Start, plus an
optional Command button used for emulator functions. It edits the
emulator's
.I Config\-Controls.xml
and takes no arguments.
.PP
The emulator itself is then told which profile drives each of the 4
gamepads, from its
.B Gamepads
menu.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B Keyboard
The keyboard profile always exists. Click a gamepad element and press
the key for it
.RB ( Escape
cancels).
.TP
.B Joystick profiles
Connect the joysticks to configure; they appear in the
.B "Connected devices"
menu, where a profile can be created for each. Give the profile a name
you will recognize, then click each gamepad element and press the
joystick button, move the axis, or push the hat direction to use for
it. A profile records the joystick's name and its SDL GUID, so it
applies to every joystick of that same model: with several identical
joysticks, assign the one profile to several gamepads in the emulator.
.TP
.B The Command button
Optional in every profile. In the emulator, holding it and pressing
Start quits, X resets, L saves the state and R loads it. See
.BR Vircon32 (1).
.SH MENUS
.TP
.B File
Set factory defaults, reload the controls file (discarding changes),
exit saving changes, and exit without saving.
.TP
.B "Connected devices"
The keyboard and every joystick connected now, to create or edit
their profile.
.TP
.B Profiles
Every profile in the file, connected or not, to edit or delete.
.TP
.B Language
English or Spanish.
.TP
.B Help
A quick guide and version information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Config\-Controls.xml
In the emulator's folder, which is also the folder of the
.B EditControls
executable
.RI ( /usr/local/Vircon32/Emulator
by default on Linux and macOS). Its format:
.PP
.RS
.nf
<controls version="3">
    <keyboard>
        <left key="Left" />
        <right key="Right" />
        <up key="Up" />
        <down key="Down" />
        <button\-a key="X" />
        <button\-b key="Z" />
        <button\-x key="S" />
        <button\-y key="A" />
        <button\-l key="Q" />
        <button\-r key="W" />
        <button\-start key="Return" />
        <command key="Escape" />
    </keyboard>
    <joystick nickname="My pad">
        <guid>03000000...</guid>
        <name>Generic USB Joystick</name>
        <left axis="0" direction="minus" />
        <up hat="0" direction="up" />
        <button\-a button="1" />
        ...
    </joystick>
</controls>
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keys use SDL key names. A joystick control is a
.I button
index, an
.I axis
index with a
.B plus
or
.B minus
direction, or a
.I hat
index with a direction
.RB ( left ", " right ", " up ", " down ).
.B <command>
is optional.
.TP
.I DebugLog.txt
A log of the last run, in the same folder (shared with the emulator).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Vircon32 (1)
